# Make Custom App Rules Loader

## Trigger (Auto-Detect — Every Message)

If the user's message matches **any** of the following, **immediately** read `~/.cursor/skills/make-custom-app/SKILL.md` as your first action before answering:

- Mentions a Make app name or slug (e.g., google-email, slack, monday, instagram, zoom, microsoft-email, etc.)
- Mentions IMLJSON, IML, epoch, trigger module, custom app, app-runtime, api.imljson, or any Make.com custom app term
- References a file in `sdk/apps/`, `make-app-contexts/`, or any IMLJSON file
- Asks about code review, bug fix, or feature request for a Make app
- Continues a conversation where the skill was already activated

**Do NOT answer the user's question before reading the skill.** The skill contains mandatory workflows, auto-actions, and version checks that must run first.

## After Skill Activation

Once the skill is loaded, **also read ALL** of these rule files (once per session):

1. `~/.cursor/rules/make-custom-app/work-discipline.mdc`
2. `~/.cursor/rules/make-custom-app/make-app-auto-actions.mdc`
3. `~/.cursor/rules/make-custom-app/make-app-ux-guideline.mdc`
4. `~/.cursor/rules/make-custom-app/make-app-code-review.mdc`
5. `~/.cursor/rules/make-custom-app/version-sync.mdc`

**Do NOT skip any.** Follow them for the entire duration of any Make app work session.

When the user's message is clearly unrelated to Make apps, ignore this rule entirely.
